wayland-server: center a fullscreen surface smaller than the screen

xdg_toplevel.set_fullscreen: a surface that does not cover the output is
centered on it and the rest filled. The server made the window the size
of the screen, then resized it to the surface's geometry at its next
commit, leaving it at the top left with the desktop beside it. Wine's
fullscreen windows of an emulated display mode (a 640x480 game on a
1920x1080 screen) present their picture at its own aspect ratio, a
1440x1080 surface: now centered on black.

The window stays the size of the screen while fullscreen; the surface's
view moves inside it, over a black view.

